dep <#1> -interface-> OUT.T@body(OUT)
dep <M> -interface-> OUT.T@R
equal F(Int) = R
== applicative applications of equal arguments share one instance
digest: checks 5 (ascription 3 argument 2) deps 6 (definition 1 instance 2 interface 3) equalities 2 omissions 0
check ascription applicative.ml:3:30-3:77 : S applicative.ml:3:36-3:77
check argument A : param(F.X)@F(A) applicative.ml:5:15-5:16
check argument A : param(F.X)@F(A) applicative.ml:6:15-6:16
check ascription M1 : S.T@R1 applicative.ml:7:19-7:42
check ascription M2 : S.T@R2 applicative.ml:8:19-8:42
dep S -definition-> <#1>
dep S.T@F(A) -instance-> S.T@body(S)
dep param(F.X)@F(A) -instance-> <param(F.X)>
dep <#1> -interface-> S.T@body(S)
dep <M1> -interface-> S.T@R1
dep <M2> -interface-> S.T@R2
equal F(A) = R1
equal F(A) = R2
== generative applications get distinct site anchors
digest: checks 3 (ascription 3) deps 6 (definition 1 instance 2 interface 3) equalities 0 omissions 0
check ascription generative.ml:3:12-3:59 : S generative.ml:3:18-3:59
check ascription M1 : S.T@R1 generative.ml:6:19-6:42
check ascription M2 : S.T@R2 generative.ml:7:19-7:42
dep S -definition-> <#1>
dep S.T@R1 -instance-> S.T@body(S)
dep S.T@R2 -instance-> S.T@body(S)
dep <#1> -interface-> S.T@body(S)
dep <M1> -interface-> S.T@R1
dep <M2> -interface-> S.T@R2
== parameter members are checked against the argument's members
digest: checks 2 (ascription 1 argument 1) deps 11 (definition 1 alias 3 instance 2 argument-member 1 interface 4) equalities 1 omissions 0
check ascription A.M : S argmember.ml:12:17-12:40
check argument A : Members@F(A) argmember.ml:14:15-14:16
dep Members -definition-> <#1>
dep Members@F(A) -instance-> Members
dep Members@F(A) -argument-member-> A.T@A
dep Members@F(A) -instance-> <Members>
dep A.T@A -alias-> S
dep Members.T@body(Members) -alias-> S
dep <Members.M> -interface-> S
dep <#1> -interface-> Members.T@body(Members)
dep <#1> -interface-> <Members.M>
dep <Members> -alias-> Members
dep <A.M> -interface-> S
equal F(A) = FA
== a strengthened parameter keeps the subject at the argument
